    output.deleteCharAt(output.length() - 1);

    return output.toString();
}
```
This code first splits the input string into individual words using the `split` method with a regular expression to match one or more whitespace characters. It then builds the output string by reversing each word using a `StringBuilder`. Finally, it removes the last character (the final space character) from the output string.

